[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247038425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247038425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247038425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JKnZ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T20:46:54Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T20:46:54Z","body":"I don't know if this was discussed on one of the earlier issues, but is it worth considering changing `is_class()` to take a `StringName` rather than adding a new `is_class_sn()`?\r\n\r\nWith a compatibility method this would be fine for GDExtension, and for within the engine and GDScript, it should be fine because `String` can automatically convert to `StringName`\r\n\r\nThe name `is_class_sn()` isn't ideal","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247038425/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247055187","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247055187","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247055187,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JOtT","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T20:49:34Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T20:50:43Z","body":"Changing `is_class` to take `StringName` would mean constructing a `StringName` every time it is called, which might not be very good\r\n\r\nThe internal code *doesn't* make any such conversions, it just compares `String` to `StringName`, avoiding any conversion (though it does do other comparisons, but they aren't necessarily significantly slower depending on the case)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247055187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247079336","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247079336","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247079336,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JUmo","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T20:53:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T20:57:26Z","body":"The name `is_class` is already not ideal, it can easily be understood as \"the object's type _is_ the class\".\r\nBut that's not true! The method checks whether the object's type is the class **or a subclass of it**.\r\nI believe `is_instance_of` or so might be better suited.\r\n\r\nThat said, there's another point I brought up last time, in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105215#issuecomment-2790931261:\r\n\r\n>  `get_class()` has been subject to a fair bit of counter-intuitive behavior regarding `class_name`, which also changed subtly over the versions: #21789\r\n> \r\n> If we already introduce a new method and suggest that users migrate away from `get_class()`, should we address some of these issues? This would be a unique opportunity to change behavior without breaking existing code.\r\n\r\nI know there's some interest to get this PR ready for the upcoming version, but could we include future fixes in a backwards-compatible way or would we then immediately need yet another method? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247079336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247099742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247099742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247099742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JZle","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T20:57:11Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T20:57:58Z","body":"> But that's not true! The method checks whether the object's type is the class or a subclass of it.\r\n\r\nExcept that's exactly how the `is` operator works, so there's precedent here, I don't think \"is\" is an incorrect use here\r\n\r\nAnd in broader polymorphism terms it is a correct definition, a `Node` *is* an `Object`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247099742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247121242","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247121242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247121242,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Je1a","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T21:00:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T21:01:11Z","body":"I decided to use `is_class_sn` because I wanted to avoid introducing another standard. We can still change to `derives_from` or `is_instance_of` or whatever in the future, but for now I think it is appropriate to stay agnostic.\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm open to exchanging `is_class` instead, with a compat function.\r\n\r\n> Changing is_class to take StringName would mean constructing a StringName every time it is called, which might not be very good\r\n> The internal code doesn't make any such conversions, it just compares String to StringName, avoiding any conversion (though it does do other comparisons, but they aren't necessarily significantly slower depending on the case)\r\n\r\nComparing `String` to `StringName` makes several memory dereferences, which is probably the bottleneck in most situations. Using `StringName` as a cached input instead both avoids a new `StringName` allocation (which is about 1/3 the cost of a `String` allocation, which is required right now btw.), and avoids the additional memory cost. It's a win in almost all situations.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247121242/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247141993","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247141993","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247141993,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79Jj5p","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T21:04:24Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T21:04:24Z","body":"> Comparing `String` to `StringName` makes several memory dereferences, which is probably the bottleneck in most situations.\r\n\r\nThat makes sense","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247141993/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247154797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247154797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247154797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JnBt","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T21:06:49Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T21:06:49Z","body":"\r\n\r\n> Except that's exactly how the `is` operator works, so there's precedent here, I don't think \"is\" is an incorrect use here\r\n\r\nIt's not incorrect, but ambiguous. Especially with `get_class()` returning the current class, it's not unreasonable to assume that\r\n```cpp\r\nobj.is_class(\"Node\")\r\n```\r\nis a shortcut for\r\n```cpp\r\nobj.get_class() == \"Node\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn top of that, what trips people over all the time are things like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/21789. If we already duplicate an existing method in `Object`, I'd say we should use the chance to clean some of the inconsistencies up and make it actually intuitive to use, meaning it works for native, GDExtension and `class_name` script classes alike...\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBut, back to topic... This PR seems to be motivated by performance, but is that worth a new method? As in, did users flag this in a way that's more important than the semantic issues?\r\n\r\nNot saying we can't fix perf without addressing all things at once, but maybe then it should change the existing method rather than add a 2nd, otherwise we soon need a 3rd :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247154797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247169552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118582#issuecomment-4247169552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118582","id":4247169552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79JqoQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T21:09:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T21:09:39Z","body":"I'd say that it is only a reasonably assumption that it is `get_class() == \"Node\"` without an understanding of polymorphism, so IMO it's not a concern that is critical to account for or anticipate, unless there's some precedent of that confusion happening?\r\n\r\nIMO a longer and bulkier name is a greater issue than a potentially confusable one that assumes not drawing the connection with the `is` operator","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247169552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4247191692","html_url":"https:/